{
  "schema": "fieldwork/caps/1",
  "note": "Every magnitude constant that can refuse a practitioner's work, declared where it can be enumerated rather than met one at a time. The practitioner, 2026-10-22, after a week of them: \"Where are these caps coming from? It seems from the outset of trying to use this widget there are caps left and right.\" and \"I have wasted 2 days with these caps.\" Six fired in sequence over two days -- a graph-limit ceiling that equalled its own default, a pre-download count that counted ways and not elements, a junction cap derived from an isochrone measurement, a 30,000-vertex geometry cap, a 100,000-character provenance cap, and a 100 km edge cap -- and each was discovered only after the cost of the previous one had been paid. Blockers and directions have had a ledger, a clock and a validator since 2026-10-12. Caps had a prose inventory (experiment 125) that listed some of them and missed the rest.\n\nEach cap here is also an individual in ontology/fieldwork.ttl, so a receipt can say which ones governed a run and at what value. A number that refuses work and cannot be queried is a number nobody can argue with.",
  "basisVocabulary": {
    "measured": "Taken from a measurement of the real thing, recorded with what was measured.",
    "derived": "Computed from a measurement, with any headroom stated.",
    "undderived": "Chosen. Says so, and carries a liftTest that would replace it with a measurement."
  },
