      "basis": "derived",
      "evidence": "A RESPONSE budget, and only that since 2026-10-22. Raised 2026-10-19 from 20,000 after a one-line probe to overpass-api.de took 14.2, 27.3 and 26.3 seconds while answering 200 every time -- which showed 20 seconds was too short and nothing more. The replacement was borrowed from OSMnx, where 180 seconds is passed to Python requests, and there it is not a limit on a download at all: requests raises only when no bytes have arrived for that long. Imported here as a total elapsed deadline it meant something else, and aborted a transfer that was working.",
