  "kindVocabulary": {
    "artefact": "Bounds something this application makes and controls: a 292-pixel drawing, a batch size, how finely a shape is approximated. Reasonable by construction -- the thing it bounds is ours, and the practitioner loses nothing they came to find.",
    "platform": "A limit the environment imposes, which this application measures and reports rather than chooses. The remedy is to name it, never to pretend it is not there.",
    "discovery": "Bounds what a practitioner can find out. These are the dangerous ones. The practitioner, 2026-10-22: \"There are reasonable caps and unreasonable ones... The others are unreasonable because they are imposing limits on things we have yet and need to discover (the DE angle).\" A number chosen here decides the answer to a question nobody has asked yet."
  },
  "chosenDiscoveryCeiling": 12,
  "ceilingRule": "It may be lowered freely and may never be raised. Widened 2026-10-22 from chosen numbers alone to every discovery cap whose basis is not a measurement. The practitioner, on finding a borrowed 180 seconds stopping a working download: \"That is the definition of an unreasonable cap, which I thought we know how to classify already.\" The classification was right -- attempt-seconds was declared discovery, derived, with a liftTest naming the measurement that would replace it -- and it bound nothing, because only undderived caps were counted. A derived number is still a number nobody measured here."
}
